  dialogueIntro:
  - I am 1, of a lineage of ancient 2, and I require a 3... Though I expect your
    skill may not be quite as refined as those of my kin, I am... willing to see
    what you can produce.
  - I am 1, 2 of the Silver Glade.  I find myself in need of a 3 for a rather delicate
    purpose. One that with heavy heart I grant to you, merchant...
  dialogueAccept:
  - Well, I certainly hope so. Most fail in my request, but I sense that you may
    possess enough skill to rise above the rabble of common merchants.
  - Hmm, how intriguing. Confidence is a rare quality among your kind. Very well,
    I shall allow you the chance to prove yourself.
  dialogueRefuse:
  - "How quaint. I had hoped to find competence in this dreary little shack, but
    it seems I\u2019ve overestimated your abilities..."
  - Do you realize what you are turning down, mortal?! Why, attempting a task of
    such importance might have broken you, both in spirit and in skill anyways.
  dialogueReturn:
  - You are once again blessed with my presence merchant... Have you prepared my
    3?
  - A
  dialogueComplete:
  - I shall use this 3 in defense of my people, and its blade will undoubtedly cut
    through lesser foes with ease.
  - "Hmm, interesting. The 3 is... serviceable. I had feared your crude methods might
    mar the flow of magic, but it seems you\u2019ve managed to avoid any grievous
    mistakes."
